<article class="env-remark" id="0ADH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ADH">Remark <span data-tag="0ADH">74.22.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $Y \to X$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $(V/Y, \varphi )$ be a descent datum relative to $Y \to X$. We may think of the isomorphism $\varphi $ as an isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (Y \times _ X Y) \times _{\text{pr}_0, Y} V \longrightarrow (Y \times _ X Y) \times _{\text{pr}_1, Y} V  \]
</div>
  <p> of algebraic spaces over $Y \times _ X Y$. So loosely speaking one may think of $\varphi $ as a map $\varphi : \text{pr}_0^*V \to \text{pr}_1^*V$<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001430995" id="a0001430995-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>. The cocycle condition then says that $\text{pr}_{02}^*\varphi = \text{pr}_{12}^*\varphi \circ \text{pr}_{01}^*\varphi $. In this way it is very similar to the case of a descent datum on quasi-coherent sheaves. </p>
</article>